.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_RESULT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_ok ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_err ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_map_ok ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_map_err ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_and_then ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_unwrap_or_else
.Nd stream helpers for Result records
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_ok "dtfl_stream *st" "const dtfl_type *ok_type"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_err "dtfl_stream *st" "const dtfl_type *err_type"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_map_ok "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_val_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_map_err "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_val_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_and_then "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_and_then_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_unwrap_or_else "dtfl_stream *st" "const dtfl_type *out_type" "dtfl_val_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These operators act on a stream of
.Em Result
records, each a tag byte
.Pq 0 for Ok, 1 for Err
followed by the arm's value.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_ok
and
.Fn dtfl_stream_err
keep only the records of one arm and emit the unwrapped value, of
.Fa ok_type
or
.Fa err_type .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_map_ok
and
.Fn dtfl_stream_map_err
transform the value of one arm with
.Fa fn ,
which writes the replacement value into the supplied buffer and returns
its length, and pass the other arm through unchanged.
The output is still a Result of the input's stream type.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_and_then
maps an Ok value to a new Result:
.Fa fn
writes the output value and sets its Ok or Err tag.
Err input records pass through.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_unwrap_or_else
emits Ok values unwrapped and turns each Err value into a value of
.Fa out_type
with
.Fa fn ,
flattening the stream to plain values.
.Pp
A value transform writes at most a few kilobytes into its buffer; a
larger value is a programming error for these helpers, which match the
small Result payloads of the pinned code.
The context in
.Fa ctx
is released by its destructor when the operator is dropped.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Each returns the new stream, owned by the stream's scope.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static size_t to_ten(void *ctx, const void *val, size_t len,
    void *out, size_t cap) {
	dtfl_put_u64(out, 10);
	return 8;
}

dtfl_stream *mapped = dtfl_stream_map_ok(results, to_ten, DTFL_NOCTX);
dtfl_stream *oks = dtfl_stream_ok(results, dtfl_type_u64());
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Fn ok ,
.Fn err ,
.Fn map_ok ,
.Fn map_err ,
.Fn and_then
and
.Fn unwrap_or_else
helpers of
.Pa vec/result.rs ,
public at the pin and removed upstream after it.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Each operator and its streams belong to the worker thread that built
them.
The callbacks run on that thread during the worker's steps.
